 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "pairs are distinct [prerequisite, course] edges of a directed acyclic graph; every course appears in at least one pair. Consider every path that starts at a course with no prerequisite and ends at a course that is no prerequisite of anything. The middle course of a path of L courses is the one at index (L-1)//2 (the left middle when L is even). Return the distinct middle courses of all such paths, sorted in code-point order.",
